        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>My car has stopped near the Bullring or on New Street — what should I do?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Put your hazard lights on, stay with the vehicle if it's safe to do so, and move yourself and any passengers well clear of moving traffic and buses. Call us with your exact location — the nearest cross street or landmark is enough — and we'll plan the quickest way in given the one-way system.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Does the Clean Air Zone affect getting my car recovered?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>No — recovering a broken-down vehicle out of the Clean Air Zone isn't a problem. The daily charge only applies to non-compliant vehicles being driven inside the Middleway, and a car on the back of a truck isn't being driven.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

